    <string name="about_title">About Papyrus by Bob</string>
    <string name="about_version">Version %1$s</string>
    <string name="about_description">A simple notepad for short notes. Notes are stored as plain text files in a folder of your choice.</string>
    <string name="about_github">GitHub: https://github.com/hjochman/Papyrus-BY-BOB</string>
    <string name="about_original">Inspired by the app “Papyrus Ex” by Kallisto (version 2.3.3, package com.kallisto.papyrusex). Papyrus by Bob is a new, independent project: the code was written from scratch, and the icon and name are original. It is not affiliated with the original developer.</string>
    <string name="about_hints_title">Notes</string>
    <string name="about_hints">• Notes are saved as .txt files. Anyone with access to the folder can read unencrypted notes.\n• Encryption (AES-256-GCM, PBKDF2) only protects the note body. The first line (title) stays readable. A forgotten password cannot be recovered.\n• To use a folder on the phone or SD card, allow access to all files in the system settings.\n• The app is provided as is, without warranty. Please back up important notes regularly.</string>
